# CloudSentinel — environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in a password:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this template is not. That split is the point of the
# file: it documents which variables exist, without carrying any of their
# values. Anyone cloning the repo can see what needs configuring, and no secret
# is ever committed to do it.
#
# SECURITY: never put a real value in this file. It is committed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL (docker-compose.yml)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Password for the local Postgres container.
#
# docker-compose.yml deliberately provides no default, so Compose refuses to
# start until this is set. Generate a random one rather than typing a memorable
# word — Node is already a dependency of this project, so no extra tool is
# needed:
#
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('hex'))"
#
# The database is bound to loopback only, so this password is not the sole thing
# standing between the internet and the data. It is still generated rather than
# guessed, because a weak local credential has a habit of being copied into the
# first non-local environment someone sets up.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Defaults shown are what docker-compose.yml falls back to.
POSTGRES_USER=cloudsentinel
POSTGRES_DB=cloudsentinel
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# Optional. Overrides how the application connects, if it needs to differ from
# the values above — pointing at a database that is not the Compose one, for
# example. When unset, lib/db/client.ts assembles the connection from the
# POSTGRES_* variables.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://cloudsentinel:password@127.0.0.1:5432/cloudsentinel

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LocalStack (collectors)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional. Where the collectors look for the simulated AWS account.
# lib/aws/localstack.ts refuses any endpoint that is not loopback, so this can
# only ever be redirected to another port on this machine — never to a real AWS
# region, and never to another host.
#
# LOCALSTACK_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4566
